{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Avenge the vengeance of the children of Israel, etc.; afterward you shall be gathered to your people</b> – It was decreed upon Moses our teacher that he not cross the Jordan, but on the far side of the Jordan he fulfilled all the commandments of Israel: he defeated the two great kings of the Amorites and divided their land as an inheritance, and it is fitting that he execute vengeance against the enemies of YHWH, while upon Joshua there remain only the commandments of the land. Moreover, the Holy One, blessed be He, apportioned him this honor, that he would see and rejoice — \"the righteous man rejoices when he sees vengeance\" — and this is the reason for \"afterward you shall be gathered to your people.\" And Moses apportioned honor to Phinehas, because he had begun the mitzvah and it was upon him to complete it, and he appointed him the anointed one for this war. And it is not fitting for Elazar to go, because he is the High Priest."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:43.742181047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}